First Author: Yeo
Title: Machine Learning for 1-Year Mortality Prediction in Lung Transplant Recipients: ISHLT Registry
Source number: 53  ￼

Very short summary: This registry-based study developed and externally validated machine-learning models for predicting 1-year mortality after lung transplantation using ISHLT data. Five key findings were: (1) 29,364 adult lung transplant recipients from the ISHLT registry were analyzed, with 16.1% dying within 1 year; (2) 25 pretransplant variables were initially identified and then reduced to the top 10 by SHAP importance without loss of performance; (3) the Gradient Boosting Machine (GBM) model achieved the best internal performance with AUC 0.958 and accuracy 0.949; (4) the simplified 10-feature GBM model maintained identical internal performance; and (5) in external validation, the in-house dataset showed reduced GBM performance (AUC 0.852, accuracy 0.764), while the multilayer perceptron showed the best generalization (AUC 0.911, accuracy 0.870). Figures 1–3 and Tables 1–4 were used directly for this extraction.  ￼

