	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The authors employed six machine-learning models, and “the GBM model achieved the highest performance.” Inputs were 25 pretransplant tabular variables from the ISHLT registry, later reduced to the top 10 using SHAP importance. External validation was performed with an in-house hospital dataset, so external geographic validation is the strongest applicable label. SHAP was explicitly used for interpretation. The text states “Default model settings were applied without additional hyperparameter tuning.”  ￼

