	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: The paper states that variables with >20% missingness were removed and “patient samples with any missing data were excluded,” which is complete-case analysis. Class imbalance was addressed using class-weight adjustments for LR, RF, SVM, and BRF. Preprocessing included exclusion criteria, feature screening, five-fold cross-validation, and SHAP-based refinement. Because the internal validation used five-fold cross-validation rather than a fixed split, training and test N are NR. No code-release statement was identified.  ￼

